  "notes": "The Liverpool/London answer to nu-jerk: jerk's staggered backbeat kept whole, but played by a drill hand. The snare still sits off the grid, only by a nudge rather than a stagger, and everything under it is UK drill discipline — an 808 that carries its own sliding counter-riff instead of doubling the kick, clean where drill's is driven, and hats that tick in triplet stutters. Over the top there is almost nothing: gloomy ambient pads, a sparse bell or piano motif, minor throughout.",
